--- fixture: data files and rows per Iceberg table
ac	2	2000
an	2	2000
mx	2	2000
pr	2	2000
pr_twin	2	2000
--- fixture: NULL counts of an.n per file; whether a file of ac has a metric for c; format and column_sizes of mx
[0,1000]
[0,1]
[('AVRO',0),('PARQUET',1)]
--- T13 an: an all-NULL file counts as NULLs, not as a file without bounds
Join: t[2000] ⋈ d[10]
ResultRows: 200
__table1.k: 2000 [min 0, max 1999]
__table1.n: 100 [min 0, max 99, null 0.5]
--- T13 ac: a file written before ADD COLUMN counts as NULLs
Join: t[2000] ⋈ d[10]
ResultRows: 400
__table1.c: 50 [min 0, max 49, null 0.5]
__table1.k: 2000 [min 0, max 1999]
--- T13 mx: no column_sizes in the Avro file and no bounds for Float64, so f takes rule 4
Join: t[2000] ⋈ d[10]
ResultRows: 33
__table1.f: 600
__table1.k: 2000 [min 0, max 1999]
--- T14 pr: MODIFY COLUMN k Int64 between the inserts, then RENAME COLUMN v TO w
Join: t[2000] ⋈ d[10]
ResultRows: 20
__table1.k: 1000 [min 0, max 999]
__table1.w: 2000 [min 0, max 1999]
--- T14 pr_twin: Int64 from the start
Join: t[2000] ⋈ d[10]
ResultRows: 20
__table1.k: 1000 [min 0, max 999]
__table1.w: 2000 [min 0, max 1999]
--- T17 use_statistics = 0: rows only
Join: t[2000] ⋈ d[no_stats~10]
ResultRows: ~~10
column entries: 0
